  <!-- ── European section ── -->
  <section class="editorial">
    <p class="section-label">Best invoicing software for European freelancers</p>
    <p>If you're based in the EU, three requirements change your tool selection: <strong>VAT fields on invoices</strong> (required by law — your VAT number, the client's VAT number for B2B, the applicable rate, and the amount), <strong>Peppol e-invoicing</strong> (mandatory in Belgium from January 2026, others following), and <strong>multi-currency</strong> support if you bill across borders.</p>
    <p><strong>Xero</strong> is the strongest choice: full Peppol support, VAT return preparation, and wide accountant adoption across the EU. <strong>Zoho Invoice</strong> is the best free alternative — multi-currency and VAT fields at no cost, though Peppol support is limited. FreshBooks, Bonsai, and QuickBooks are primarily US-built and lack Peppol integration entirely.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ── How to choose ── -->
  <section class="editorial">
    <p class="section-label">How to choose</p>
    <div class="decision-grid">
      <div class="decision-card">
        <p class="decision-q">Do you need accounting too, or just invoicing?</p>
        <p class="decision-a">If you have an accountant, choose Xero — they can access your books directly. Otherwise, FreshBooks or Wave give you enough without the complexity.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="decision-card">
        <p class="decision-q">Do you bill by the hour?</p>
        <p class="decision-a">Use Harvest. The time-to-invoice workflow is the cleanest in this category and saves real hours every month.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="decision-card">
        <p class="decision-q">Are you in Europe and need VAT compliance?</p>
        <p class="decision-a">Xero is the answer. Zoho Invoice works as a free alternative if VAT fields and multi-currency are the only requirements.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="decision-card">
        <p class="decision-q">What is your budget?</p>
        <p class="decision-a">Zero: Wave or Zoho Invoice. Under $25/mo: FreshBooks Lite or QuickBooks (US only). Need everything in one: Bonsai Essentials.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="callout"><strong>FreshBooks vs Xero:</strong> Choose FreshBooks for the cleanest invoicing UX in one currency. Choose Xero if you work with an accountant, bill internationally, or are based in Europe. <a href="/freshbooks-vs-xero-for-freelancers/">See our full comparison →</a></p>
  </section>

  <!-- ── FAQ ── -->
  <section class="editorial">
    <p class="section-label">Frequently asked questions</p>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What is the best free invoicing software for freelancers?</summary>
        <p>Zoho Invoice and Wave are the two strongest free options. Zoho Invoice has more automation (recurring invoices, reminders, client portal) and supports multi-currency at no cost. Wave adds double-entry bookkeeping with no invoice cap. Both are permanently free, not trials.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is FreshBooks worth it for freelancers?</summary>
        <p>Yes, for most freelancers who invoice more than a handful of clients per month. The automation — late payment reminders, recurring invoices, automatic late fees — saves two to three hours a month. The 5-client cap on the $23/month Lite plan is the main friction point.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What invoicing software works best for European freelancers?</summary>
        <p>Xero. It supports VAT returns, Peppol e-invoicing, and multi-currency — the three requirements that matter most in EU markets. Zoho Invoice is the best free alternative if you need VAT fields and multi-currency but can't justify a paid plan yet.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I use QuickBooks just for invoicing?</summary>
        <p>You can, but it's expensive for what you get if invoicing is the only need. QuickBooks Solopreneur at $20/month makes most sense for US freelancers who want invoicing tied to quarterly tax estimates and TurboTax. For invoicing alone, FreshBooks or Wave are better fits.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

